{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Historical description-size calibration (2026-08-10) — operator-directed blocking limit\n\nMethod: replayed CREATE/EDIT history, including retired events, for every bug/story/task/epic in the tracker. For each plan-review and completion-verifier sidecar, reconstructed the authoritative description length at that event timestamp. Corpus: 2,202 work tickets, 4,037 plan-review events, and 1,121 completion-verifier events. This avoids using only current text after later edits.\n\nDistribution across work tickets: p50 1,844 chars; p75 3,031; p90 4,477; p95 5,331; p97.5 6,337; p99 7,500; maximum 15,853. The current 24,000-character cap is above the historical maximum and therefore cannot protect either gate.\n\nCandidate 8,000-character cutoff: 18/2,202 current work tickets (0.82%) meet or exceed it. Plan review at >=8,000 chars: 41 events across 8 tickets, median 553.7s and p90 981.9s, versus 389.5s/p90 711.2s below the cutoff. Completion verification at >=8,000 chars: 14 events with 50.0% PASS, versus 74.3% below; first-attempt PASS was 57.1% across 7 tickets, versus 73.7% below. At >=10,000 the signal is stronger but the sample shrinks to two reviewed tickets and would miss the 8–10K pain range. At 6,000 the signal exists but would block 3.18% of work tickets, which is unnecessarily broad.\n\nDecision: set the default maximum description length to 8,000 characters and make exceeding it BLOCKING. This is a generous tail limit just above p99, not a normal-writing target. It should apply before both plan review and completion verification so an oversized ticket is decomposed before consuming a gate run. Keep the value config-driven. The ticket description's prior requirements that P4 remain advisory/never block are superseded by this operator decision and must be revised before implementation.\n\nLimits: description length correlates with ticket complexity, so the history does not prove length alone causes every failure. The cutoff is justified operationally: it touches <1% of tickets while capturing the range with materially worse wall time and completion reliability."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786394876204352001,"uuid":"e6abc4bc-dd92-44c9-8905-d6db8db49c51"}